Because object prop look same, but is new object every render.

React compare props by reference, not deep contents. So this:

```jsx
<Child config={{ theme: "dark" }} />
```

make brand new object on every parent render. `Child` see new `config` reference, so it re-renders even if values same.

Fix by keeping object reference stable:

```jsx
const config = useMemo(() => ({ theme: "dark" }), []);
return <Child config={config} />;
```

Or define it outside component if truly static:

```jsx
const config = { theme: "dark" };
```

Also note:
- If child is not wrapped in `React.memo`, it re-renders whenever parent re-renders anyway.
- `React.memo` only helps when prop references stay stable.

Typical pattern:

```jsx
const Child = React.memo(function Child({ config }) {
  ...
});

function Parent({ count }) {
  const config = useMemo(() => ({ theme: "dark" }), []);
  return <Child config={config} />;
}
```

