Use `pg`’s `Pool` with three layers of protection:

1. pool-level limits so you do not overload Postgres
2. connect/query timeouts so callers do not hang forever
3. central error handling so bad clients get released and background pool errors are visible

Example:

```js
// db.js
const { Pool } = require('pg');

const pool = new Pool({
